1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:03,640
Raheel Tesmiferium, can I get something off my chest?

2
00:00:04,520 --> 00:00:06,340
Black fame and wealth are not synonymous

3
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:07,220
with black excellence.

4
00:00:07,420 --> 00:00:10,080
Materialism was not our ancestors' wildest dreams

5
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:13,040
and social media influencers can't, nor should ever,

6
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:16,380
be our guiding light and measure of greatness.

7
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:19,180
21st century black excellence should still be rooted

8
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:21,480
in the liberation of our people.

9
00:00:21,620 --> 00:00:24,280
Otherwise it's just capitalism masquerading

10
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:26,240
as the promised land.

11
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:28,400
Pure unadulterated facts.

12
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:34,640
Capitalist success is not a signifier of liberation for all.

13
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:35,880
It's not.

14
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:41,380
And it's not a signifier for someone being so much more connected

15
00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:43,080
to their ancestors than someone else.

16
00:00:43,660 --> 00:00:45,300
And we do this all the time.

17
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:48,020
We look at people who have reached a certain level of fame

18
00:00:48,020 --> 00:00:50,460
and money and wealth and we say, wow, look at them.

19
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:52,500
Churches are even preaching that as a word.

20
00:00:53,820 --> 00:00:56,460
Don't get me wrong, money is a delightful enabler,

21
00:00:56,460 --> 00:00:59,240
but it will not save us if we don't know us.

